Imports:
  - Types:
      - LazyLoader
    From: salt/loader

Annotations: |
  This cell is salt/runners — 31 master-side orchestration modules. Unlike salt/modules,
  runner functions execute exclusively on the master (via salt.loader.runner, tag
  "runners", packed as __salt__ — a distinct `LazyLoader` from the minion-side one built by
  minion_mods) and read master-side state (job caches, the key store, presence data) rather
  than talking to a live minion transport directly. This CODEMANIFEST documents 5 representative
  real functions out of 31 files.

---

"active(display_progress: bool) -> jobs:dict[str, object]":
  location: jobs.py
  annotations: |
    Return currently in-flight jobs across all minions, by scanning the configured returner's job
    cache for jobs that have not yet reported back from every targeted minion.

"list_jobs(ext_source: str | None, outputter: str | None, search_metadata: dict[str, object] | None, search_function: str | None, search_target: str | None, start_time: str | None, end_time: str | None, display_progress: bool) -> jobs:dict[str, object]":
  location: jobs.py
  annotations: |
    List jobs recorded in the job cache, optionally filtered.

    `ext_source`: which returner to read the job cache from, overriding the configured default
    `search_metadata`: only return jobs whose metadata matches this mapping
    `search_function`: only return jobs that called this function name
    `search_target`: only return jobs targeted at this minion/glob
    `start_time`, `end_time`: only return jobs started within this window

"lookup_jid(jid: str, ext_source: str | None, returned: bool, missing: bool, display_progress: bool) -> result:dict[str, object]":
  location: jobs.py
  annotations: |
    Return the full result set for one previously run job.

    `jid`: the job id to look up
    `returned`: include minions that returned a result
    `missing`: include minions that were targeted but never returned

"status(output: bool, tgt: str, tgt_type: str, timeout: int | None, gather_job_timeout: int | None) -> status:dict[str, list[str]]":
  location: manage.py
  annotations: |
    Report which minions matching `tgt`/`tgt_type` are currently reachable versus unresponsive, by
    issuing a live ping and comparing against the configured minion key set.

"safe_accept(target: str, tgt_type: str) -> outcome:str":
  location: manage.py
  annotations: |
    Accept the specified pending minion key(s) only after first confirming (via a fingerprint
    round-trip) that the key actually belongs to a live, reachable minion — safer than a blind
    salt-key -A.

    `target`: minion id or glob/pattern of pending keys to accept
    `tgt_type`: how to interpret `target` (glob, list, etc.)
    `outcome`: human-readable summary of which keys were accepted versus rejected

